  "title": "Yijing's sea voyage to Srivijaya and India",
  "summary": "In 671 the Chinese monk Yijing sailed from Guangzhou on a Persian merchant ship to Srivijaya, a trading kingdom most probably centred on Palembang. He went on to eastern India and spent about nine years at Nalanda, returned to Srivijaya in 687, and reached Luoyang in 695.",
